                <pb facs="0511" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.00/587: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Iraq</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-28T17:00:00+03:00">April 28, 1941—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>103. Referring my 97, April 24.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d520-f1"/> Saw Foreign
                    Minister today informing him I had been authorized establish informal contact
                    with him. He did not press for anything further at this juncture.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
